  "open_questions": [
    "Msg 0x044d ('* ROSTER FULL *') exists in msg.dbs but no push of this value was found in any .ovr file or wroot.exe via static pattern scan. When create_via_empty_slot finds no empty slot (roster_find_first_empty_slot returns 0=none), the function simply returns without displaying any error message. Possible explanations: (a) the caller (wpcmk_show_roster_picker) handles the case before calling; (b) the message is truly unused in Wiz6 and was carried over from a prior game version; (c) it is displayed via a dynamic message_base+offset calculation not captured by static scan.",
    "Msg 0x0261 ('     PRESS \\x15 TO EXIT     ') is displayed at site 0x1344 in ui_class_menu_with_qualification when on the LAST skill category (conditional branch at 0x1344: cmp ax; jle -> 0x0261 vs 0x0260). The exact branch condition was not verified in this pass.",
    "The 0x1941 site in creation_stage_dispatcher_by_step shows skill_category_names (base 0x0258). The exact mapping of [bp+8] (a parameter) to which category is selected has not been traced — this requires understanding the creation step dispatcher's caller in ui_welcome_animation (0x1ae9) which passes the step index. This determines which category label appears on which pass of the spell-school animation.",
    "FUN_5011 (called at 0x5199 from create_via_empty_slot) is NOT the same as the modal error display FUN_505b. FUN_5011 appears to be a roster-slot scanner that reads and checks slot names. The call at 0x5079 inside FUN_5011 writes the msg_id from [bp+4] (a passed argument). The caller at 0x5199 pushes ax (result of text_input_editor at 0x5183) so the msg_id argument is unclear. FUN_5011 may show a name-match or roster header message; full decompile needed.",
    "The wpcmk_show_roster_picker at 0x56a0 contains two calls to ui_window_write_chars (0xdf85) and multiple calls to ui_window_put_char_repeat (0xdd53) and ui_window_puts (0xdfb9). These draw decorative borders and separators (not msg.dbs messages). Not itemized in findings to avoid clutter.",
    "Msg 0x0256 ('YOU EARNED A SKILL BONUS!') appears at base+5 from 0x0258 but it's unclear which skill categories trigger this special message vs. the category header at base+0..3. The 'EXIT' category at base+4 (0x025c) is also unusual.",
    "Screen-04-bonus-roller and screen-07-derived-stats are confirmed non-interactive and display no msg.dbs strings (only stat panel redraws via ui_render_stat_panel which IS covered). Screen-01-init shows the creation panel borders via ui_draw_creation_screen_borders (0x06af) which uses styled chars (0x0689 ui_put_styled_char_at), not msg.dbs strings.",
    "Screen-11-class-starter-items and screen-16-save are non-interactive and use no string display functions (confirmed by byte scan showing no 0xc2db or 0xc1f7 calls in those address ranges 0x3c49..0x3e8b and 0x4fab..0x4ff3).",
    "The 'SPELLS' title at 0x02bc (site 0x1d93 in ui_draw_train_screen_borders) may also display in ui_class_menu_with_qualification during spell school animation. The exact conditions under which this title appears vs. a skill category title (0x0258+) need to be traced from the creation_stage_dispatcher caller chain."
  ],

